<title>SRI LANKA: Ceylon Tobacco down on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Ceylon Tobacco down on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Ceylon Tobacco Company fell 3.03 percent or one rupee to 32 on Monday on profit-taking by small investors, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Small retail investors are probably raising cash,&quot; said a broker who declined to be identified.</p>
<p>The blue chip Ceylon Tobacco Ltd, Sri Lanka's monopoly cigarette maker, is a subsidiary of BAT Industries Plc.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
